**Definition 2.3 (actual initial installation).** Execute ARC Definitions
4.1–4.3 with $G_{\rm sel}$ replacing $G$ throughout. Pay for the ten L/R
pairs and their owner/phase bits; keep the single original preparation and
stationary acquisition. The two fresh bootstraps receive respectively
$E(L)$ and $E(G_{\rm sel})$. Between them the native capture-only $L$
actually receives

$$
101\,U(\delta_{\rm sel})\,\Delta(G_{\rm sel}),\qquad
\delta_{\rm sel}=|\Delta(G_{\rm sel})|.
$$

$E$ is the installation serialization and $\Delta$ the framed row/effect/
entry description; RCA's finite serializer connects them. The strings
are different objects. Capture69 has its unique sentinel F, base one,
descriptor ordinal zero and payload length $2\delta_{\rm sel}+4$.
$L$ contains neither the main description nor its length. The main graph
reads its own description only from this actual captured field, not a
self-description constant.

In the captured description's finite entry component retain the original
entries and append two fixed slots, SourceEntrySet and SourceExitSet.
Each is an encoded list of the two parity alternatives, each item a tuple
of version tag, pre-row state number and successor state number. The
assembler obtains these numbers from the symbolic edges of Definition
5.3 after the graph is expanded/numbered. The entry parser reads these
two slots in their fixed order, validates arity/ranges, and resolves every
item to the unique decoded CTL row with that successor and appropriate
fixed local phase effect. The main program obtains these words only by
Nth/ReadList on its actual captured description. This is finite entry
metadata, erased with the other entry framing when emitting $E$; it is
not code that emits an unknown unary numeral for its own row address.
The source edges have symbolic targets before this numbering, so neither
graph construction nor register count depends on the digits of these
metadata numbers. Their actual bits and validation work are paid.

On main entry append bank sentinels, unroll exactly $r_{\rm sel}$ empty
fields in the ARC empty-bank prelude, describe/seal bank64 and set parity A.
Initialize sentinels70–73, without a second sentinel69. Append ARC's fixed
ordered initial69 fields: actual public/prior/controller/boot bindings;
finite earlier graph/boot/$L$ descriptions; actual acquired seed and its
delivery origin; closed28/29 imports with preactivation dependencies; and
saved26/28/29 head table with its fixed activation position. Restore those
heads. ManifestPrefix starts Home69; MR; MR, imports the entire closed
initial prefix before later staging, validates field zero and its entries,
then initializes $M$, cover/package lists and the new persistent fields.
They start empty, with a distinguished unset mode; no request uses an
unset field. Actual TOK to the outer client and Ready CTL establish the
first $R_r$. Canonical supply of all these bits is a premise, not a silent
change to a running $G$.

